  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 246 PM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nNot much change from the previous forecast mid-level high \npressure will build over the next couple of days from the east\nwhich will be taking over by midweek. Expect this to promote warm\nand mostly rain free conditions outside of seabreeze convection. \nWill need to monitor the possibility for some short-fused heat \nrelated products. We could see heat indices up to 115 as early as \ntomorrow with dew points around the mid to upper 70s present \nthrough the next week. This translates to Moderate to Major heat \nstress conditions. We strongly encourage the practice of heat \nsafety in these conditions. Take frequent breaks and remember to \nstay hydrated, check those backseats, and avoid long exposure in \nthese temperatures. For more information be sure to check out \nweather.gov/heatsafety.",
